1	//! `derrick-hand` — a generic host-CLI [`HandDispatcher`].
2	//!
3	//! [`HostCliHandDispatcher`] drives any of derrick's host CLIs (codex,
4	//! opencode, aider, …) as a crew-mode executor hand. It mirrors the shape of
5	//! `derrick_copilot::LocalCopilotHandDispatcher`: per ticket it creates a git
6	//! worktree on the ticket's branch (rooted at the foreman-supplied parent
7	//! branch) and runs the host CLI there, so concurrently dispatched hands never
8	//! share a checkout or index. It routes through the shared [`HostRegistry`]
9	//! instead of spawning a process directly, so model forwarding and per-host
10	//! CLI normalisation (D65) happen inside the adapter.
11	//!
12	//! The model id is threaded RAW (`provider/model` or a bare id) into
13	//! [`HostRequest::model`]; the adapter calls `catalogue::normalize` per host.
14	//! Crucially, a ticket never reaches `Done` from a hand self-report: this
15	//! dispatcher only ever moves `Ready → InFlight` (via `assign_to_hand`) and
16	//! leaves the merge-observed transition to the foreman's verifier (D31/D32).
17	
18	use std::path::PathBuf;
19	use std::sync::Arc;
20	use std::time::Duration;
21	
22	use async_trait::async_trait;
23	use chrono::Utc;
24	use derrick_substrate::{
25	    EventKind, EventScope, Hand, HandId, HandKind, Substrate, SubstrateError, Ticket,
26	};
27	use derrick_substrate_native::foreman::{
28	    DispatchContext, DispatchError, DispatchResult, HandDispatcher,
29	};
30	use derrick_substrate_native::NativeSubstrate;
31	use derrick_tools::{HostRegistry, HostRequest};
32	use tokio::process::Command;
33	use tracing::{info, instrument, warn};
